---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MetricCard from "../../components/MetricCard.astro";
import ResultTable from "../../components/ResultTable.astro";
import Figure from "../../components/Figure.astro";
import { external } from "../../data/site";
import { percent, readCsv } from "../../lib/csv";
import food101 from "../../../assignments/assignment-2/proposal/food-101.jpg";
import eda from "../../../assignments/assignment-2/source/results/eda_samples.png";
import curves from "../../../assignments/assignment-2/source/results/all_models_curves.png";
import confusion from "../../../assignments/assignment-2/source/results/cm_resnet50_full_finetune.png";
import gradcam from "../../../assignments/assignment-2/source/results/gradcam_comparison.png";

const results = readCsv("assignments/assignment-2/source/results/comparison_summary.csv", ["Model", "Total_Params", "Trainable_Params", "Test_Acc", "Test_Macro_F1", "Train_Time_s", "Latency_ms_Per_Img"]);
const ablation = readCsv("assignments/assignment-2/source/results/ablation_augmentation_summary.csv", ["Configuration", "Test_Acc", "Test_Macro_F1", "Train_Time_s"]);
---
<BaseLayout title="Assignment 2" description="Food-101 specialized image classification for CO3133 Assignment 2." current="a2">
  <section class="shell page-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Assignment 2 · Specialized vision</p><div class="page-status"><span class="status status-active">Proposal + implementation available</span><small>Dataset approval, final report, slides, and YouTube video remain pending.</small></div><h1>Deep Learning on Large-Scale Data and Specialized Tasks</h1><p class="page-lead">Fine-grained Food-101 image classification using a reproducible ten-class subset, a custom CNN baseline, and two-stage ResNet-50 transfer learning.</p></section>
  <section class="shell"><div class="metric-grid"><MetricCard label="Full fine-tuning" value="88.80%" detail="ResNet-50 test accuracy" accent={true} /><MetricCard label="Frozen backbone" value="80.24%" detail="ResNet-50 test accuracy" /><MetricCard label="Custom CNN" value="63.36%" detail="Trained-from-scratch test accuracy" /></div></section>
  <section class="shell article-layout"><article><section class="article-section"><h2>Problem statement</h2><p>Given one RGB food image, predict one category from a fixed ten-class Food-101 subset. The study evaluates the performance and compute trade-offs between a self-implemented CNN and pretrained ResNet-50 under controlled data and evaluation conditions.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Dataset description and EDA</h2><p>The alphabetical ten-class subset contains 7,500 official training images and 2,500 official test images. The official test split remains untouched; the official training split is stratified into 6,750 training and 750 validation images with seed 42. EDA covers class balance, dimensions, representative images, readability, exact hashing, and perceptual-duplicate auditing.</p><div class="result-grid"><Figure src={food101} alt="Food-101 food-image montage" caption="Food-101 illustration from the dataset website." /><Figure src={eda} alt="Representative Food-101 samples from the selected classes" caption="Selected Food-101 subset: representative images used in EDA." /></div></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Methodology</h2><p>The baseline is a four-block custom CNN trained from scratch. The transfer-learning comparison uses ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-50 with a new ten-class classifier, evaluated first with a frozen backbone and then with a five-epoch warm-up followed by full fine-tuning. Inputs are 224×224 RGB tensors normalized with ImageNet statistics.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Experimental setup</h2><p>All comparisons use the same fixed classes, image-level split, seed, preprocessing, metrics, and validation-Macro-F1 checkpoint rule. The implementation records parameter counts, training time, latency, and peak GPU memory alongside accuracy and Macro-F1.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Results</h2><p>Full ResNet-50 fine-tuning produces the strongest primary result. The table below is read directly from the experiment summary CSV.</p><ResultTable caption="Food-101 ten-class controlled comparison" rows={results} columns={[{key:"Model",label:"Model"},{key:"Total_Params",label:"Total parameters"},{key:"Trainable_Params",label:"Trainable"},{key:"Test_Acc",label:"Test accuracy",format:percent},{key:"Test_Macro_F1",label:"Macro-F1",format:percent},{key:"Latency_ms_Per_Img",label:"Latency / image",format:(value) => `${value} ms`}]} /><div class="result-grid"><Figure src={curves} alt="Training and validation curves for Assignment 2 models" caption="Training behavior for the custom CNN and ResNet-50 configurations." /><Figure src={confusion} alt="Confusion matrix for fully fine-tuned ResNet-50" caption="Fine-tuned ResNet-50 confusion matrix on the untouched official test split." /></div></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Comparison and discussion</h2><p>Transfer learning substantially improves the specialized classification result over the custom baseline. The secondary augmentation ablation records a higher result without augmentation in this single configuration; it is an observed result, not a general claim that augmentation is harmful.</p><ResultTable caption="Secondary augmentation ablation" rows={ablation} columns={[{key:"Configuration",label:"Configuration"},{key:"Test_Acc",label:"Test accuracy",format:percent},{key:"Test_Macro_F1",label:"Macro-F1",format:percent},{key:"Train_Time_s",label:"Train time",format:(value) => `${value}s`}]} /></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Error analysis</h2><p>Per-class metrics, top-confused pairs, qualitative prediction grids, and Grad-CAM overlays support analysis of visually similar categories and model attention. The final report will consolidate the written taxonomy and examples.</p><div class="result-grid"><Figure src={gradcam} alt="Grad-CAM comparison across custom CNN and ResNet-50 models" caption="Grad-CAM comparison of the completed model configurations." /></div></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Limitations and conclusion</h2><p>All conclusions apply only to the selected ten Food-101 classes. Relevant limitations include noisy labels, class similarity, the fixed image-resolution pipeline, and the available compute budget for fine-tuning.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Assignment-specific AI Usage Disclosure</h2><p>Four documented Google Gemini uses supported integrity auditing, hardware measurements, Grad-CAM, qualitative-analysis figures, and report formatting. Each use records responsible member, verification, and source material. <a href={external.a2Ai}>Read the complete Assignment 2 log.</a></p></section></article><aside class="side-stack"><section class="resource-card"><p class="eyebrow">Resources</p><h2>Deliverables</h2><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2Source}><span>Source code</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2Readme}><span>Reproduction & checkpoints</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2Results}><span>All result artifacts</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2Proposal}><span>Dataset proposal</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2ProposalPdf}><span>Formatted proposal PDF</span><b>Open ↗</b></a><div class="pending">Instructor approval · pending</div><div class="pending">Final report · pending</div><div class="pending">Slides · pending</div><div class="pending">YouTube video · pending</div><a class="resource-link" href={external.a2Ai}><span>AI disclosure</span><b>Open ↗</b></a></section></aside></section>
</BaseLayout>
